<p>If you want to replace Gmail as your email provider, start with Outlook.com for the Microsoft ecosystem, Proton Mail or Tuta Mail for privacy-focused email, Zoho Mail or Fastmail for a custom domain, and iCloud Mail if you live in Apple's ecosystem. Yahoo Mail is another familiar consumer option. If you only want a different inbox interface, a mail app can still connect to Gmail without moving your mailbox. These seven alternatives solve different problems, so the right choice depends on storage, domain needs, privacy goals and how much migration work you can accept.</p>
<p>One current detail matters before you switch: Google is removing Gmail web support for POP and Gmailify access to third-party accounts, and the third-party “Send as” feature ends in January 2027. Existing POP/Gmailify users can continue until January 2027, while new users lost access after the first quarter of 2026. Read Google's <a href="https://support.google.com/mail/answer/16604719?hl=en">POP/Gmailify notice</a> and <a href="https://support.google.com/mail/answer/22370?hl=en">Send as notice</a>, checked on November 1, 2026.</p>
<h2 id="quick-comparison">Quick comparison of Gmail alternatives</h2>
